  "implementation": [
    "Observe canonical object selection from actual production stellar surface, verified nebula texture/plane and constellation-line render callbacks; preserve route and raw asset hash binding.",
    "Capture same-scene baseline/active/returned object identities, loading failures, publication revisions and timestamps; reject stale callbacks, mismatched targets, failed cleanup, unknown JSON shapes and cross-build observations.",
    "Distinguish exact registered resource reuse from actual acquire/release. Only actual observed disposal may satisfy the separate release lifecycle gate.",
    "Register nebula plane and constellation allocations; track existing stellar geometry/material owners through real THREE disposal events without taking over disposal or treating unmount as release. Stable semantic slots permit valid baseline restoration.",
    "Export up to 48 local observations; intake explicit raw files with exact byte hashes into an exclusive-write candidate index, replay all 36 manifest objects and require separate current-build browser evidence.",
    "Evaluate two independent same-build, same-viewport, non-overlapping runs of at least 30 minutes; validate continuous visibility, RAF coverage, phase timeline/checkpoint correspondence and released resources.",
    "Use Windows-compatible ESM loader file URLs so release subprocess tests exercise actual raw replay, not startup failure."
  ],
